;; Regulatory source register for JPN-STATISTICS official-statistics
;; reporting-obligation compliance.
;;
;; README.md says: every regulatory claim must cite the official Statistics
;; Japan source. docs/operator-guide.md requires clear provenance for every
;; requirement surfaced. docs/business-model.md makes a fabricated regulatory
;; claim a HARD hold that must be corrected against a cited source first.
;;
;; Until this file existed there was no such list. Three documents required a
;; citation against a set that did not exist, so no claim in this repository
;; could be traced to anything, and nothing could tell a real citation from an
;; invented one. This is that list.
;;
;; Shape is tx-data (a vector of entity maps), like every other EDN corpus in
;; this workspace, so it loads with
;;   (d/transact conn (edn/read-string (slurp "facts.edn")))
;; :source/id is the join key. A law not in this table has NO spec-basis for
;; this repository -- extend the table, never invent an id or a URL.
;;
;; VERIFIED BY `nbb scripts/verify-facts.cljk`, which re-fetches every entry
;; from the live authority. Each entry carries a :source/verify tag naming
;; WHICH check establishes it. The checks are not interchangeable, and the
;; reasons are the main thing this file has to teach.
;;
;; ── THE AUTHORITY THIS REPOSITORY NAMES IS NOT THE ONE THAT RUNS THE
;;    OBLIGATION MACHINERY
;;
;; organization.edn names 総務省統計局 and gives www.stat.go.jp. That is the
;; survey-and-data side. The approval, notification and review machinery under
;; 統計法 -- the part an operator with a reporting obligation actually meets --
;; is run by 政策統括官（統計制度担当）, a different part of the same ministry,
;; and it is published on www.soumu.go.jp/toukei_toukatsu/.
;;
;; So this register spans two hosts of one ministry plus the statistics portal,
;; and they do not behave alike. Measured 2026-08-27:
;;
;;   www.soumu.go.jp    Shift_JIS   no charset in header   404 distinctive
;;   www.stat.go.jp     Shift_JIS   no charset in header   404 titled like
;;                                                         the front page
;;   www.e-stat.go.jp   UTF-8       charset IS in header   404 distinctive
;;
;; A verifier written against any one of them is wrong about the other two.
;; :host/charset is declared per HOST for exactly this reason.
;;
;; ── SHIFT_JIS WITH NO CHARSET IN THE HEADER, ON TWO OF THE THREE HOSTS
;;
;; Both ministry hosts answer Content-Type: text/html with NO charset
;; parameter, and the bytes are Shift_JIS. The encoding is declared only in
;; the HTML meta.
;;
;; A verifier that reads the body with res.text() gets UTF-8 decoding, which
;; on these bytes produces deterministic mojibake. Measured, for the live
;; 統計法について page whose real title is 総務省｜統計制度｜統計法について:
;;
;;   res.text()  ->  title 「�����ȁb���v���x�b���v�@�ɂ���」
;;
;; That is not a crash and not an empty string. It is a stable, plausible-
;; looking value, and it breaks the register in BOTH directions:
;;
;;   - Every Japanese :page/must-contain needle fails to match, so every live
;;     page in this register would be reported as a dead citation.
;;   - An author who filled in :page/title by pasting what the verifier
;;     printed would pin the mojibake, and the check would then pass forever
;;     while asserting nothing about the page.
;;
;; So the body is decoded with :host/charset, and the run re-reads each page's
;; own meta charset and REFUSES if it no longer agrees with the host
;; declaration -- because the day these hosts migrate to UTF-8 is the day every
;; stored title in this file becomes wrong at once, and that must surface as
;; REFUSED (the register is out of date) and not as twelve page failures (the
;; pages are gone).
;;
;; ── www.stat.go.jp SERVES ITS 404 UNDER THE FRONT PAGE'S OWN TITLE
;;
;; This is the sharpest host finding here and it has no counterpart on the
;; other two hosts. Measured 2026-08-27:
;;
;;   https://www.stat.go.jp/index.html                 200  36,963 B
;;   https://www.stat.go.jp/no-such-page-zzz999...     404   4,691 B
;;
;;   ...and BOTH carry <title>統計局ホームページ</title>.
;;
;; The bodies differ and the status differs, so a dead citation is still
;; detectable -- on status. But the TITLE conjunct is vacuous for any entry
;; that cites a page titled 統計局ホームページ: the check would pass on a URL
;; that does not exist. That is the same defect as a needle that sits on the
;; 404 chrome, and it is treated the same way -- as a finding about the
;; register, not about the page.
;;
;; This is why the front page is NOT in this register. /data/index.html and
;; /info/guide/index.html are, because their titles carry a suffix
;; (統計局ホームページ/統計データ) that the 404 body does not have. The run
;; FAILS any page entry whose declared title equals its host's missing-page
;; title, with reason :title-on-missing-page, before the page is fetched.
;;
;; The collision itself is re-measured every run: the preflight requires the
;; 404 title and the known-real-path title to still be equal. If Statistics
;; Japan ever gives its 404 page a title of its own, this rule has expired and
;; that is the check which notices.
;;
;; ── THE MISSING-PAGE BODY CARRIES THIS REPOSITORY'S OWN HQ ADDRESS
;;
;; Measured present on www.stat.go.jp's 404 body, for a URL that does not
;; exist:
;;
;;   統計局   総務省   若松町   162-8668   03-5273-2020
;;
;; organization.edn asserts Wakamatsuchō as the HQ line. So the obvious way to
;; confirm the address -- fetch a stat.go.jp page and look for 若松町, or for
;; the postcode -- passes on a page that is not there. The 404 body is only
;; 4,691 bytes and still finds room for the full footer.
;;
;; www.soumu.go.jp's 404 body is ~39 KB of site chrome and carries 届出,
;; 統計情報, 個人情報 and 100-8926. 届出 is one of the entry routes under
;; 統計法, so the obvious sentinel for a notification-procedure page is on the
;; missing-page body of the host that publishes it.
;;
;; www.e-stat.go.jp's 404 body carries e-Stat and 政府統計の総合窓口 -- the
;; portal's own name, and the exact title of its front page. The obvious
;; sentinel for 「this is e-Stat」 is on the page that says e-Stat could not
;; find what you asked for.
;;
;; The verifier does not leave that to whoever writes the next entry. It
;; fetches each host's missing-page body once and FAILS any :page/must-contain
;; string found on it, with reason :chrome-needle, before the cited page is
;; fetched at all.
;;
;; ── TWO ORDINANCES SHARE ONE TITLE AND ONE OF THEM IS REPEALED
;;
;; 経済センサス基礎調査規則 names two different instruments:
;;
;;   420M60000008125  平成二十年総務省令第百二十五号   REPEALED 2019-04-01
;;   431M60000008046  平成三十一年総務省令第四十六号   in force
;;
;; A citer who writes down the title 経済センサス基礎調査規則 and gets a title
;; match has established nothing about which ordinance they cited. Title
;; checking is not merely weak here -- it is provably unable to separate a live
;; designated-survey ordinance from one repealed seven years ago, for a survey
;; that businesses are actually enumerated in.
;;
;; So every statute entry declares :egov/law-num as well as :egov/law-title,
;; and the two of them have separate negative controls in the self-tests: the
;; repealed ordinance declared in force with its title AND number left correct
;; (only :egov/repeal-status can catch it), and the live ordinance declared
;; with the repealed one's law number (only :egov/law-num can catch it, since
;; title, repeal status and revision status all match).
;;
;; 工業統計調査規則 and 商業統計調査規則 are carried for the same reason: both
;; were real designated-survey ordinances, both were repealed into the economic
;; census, and both still answer the API with the title and law number a citer
;; would have written down.
;;
;; ── AND A LIVE ACT CAN FAIL A SECOND WAY THE REPEAL FIELD DOES NOT SEE
;;
;; 421AC0000000066, 公文書等の管理に関する法律 -- which governs how the records
;; an operator submits are kept -- has repeal_status None but
;; current_revision_status PreviousEnforced. The displayed revision is not the
;; enforced one. Both fields are declared per entry and both are checked.
;;
;; NOT remain_in_force: that field reads like the answer and is not. Measured
;; 2026-08-27 on 統計法 itself, live and in force, remain_in_force is false --
;; the same value the repealed 経済センサス基礎調査規則 carries. Keying on it
;; would mark every live statute in this register dead. It also lives under
;; revision_info, not law_info, so reading it from the obvious place returns
;; nil, which is a third wrong answer that looks like a missing field.
;;
;; ── laws.e-gov.go.jp CANNOT BE CHECKED AS A PAGE AT ALL
;;
;; Measured 2026-08-27 with this repository's own core statute:
;; /law/419AC0000000053 (統計法, real) and /law/999ZZ9999999999 (invented) both
;; answer HTTP 200, at the requested URL with no redirect, with the identical
;; title e-Gov 法令検索 over a small client-rendered shell, at the identical
;; 800 bytes. Status, final URL, title and length all agree between a real
;; citation and a fabricated one. The length is deliberately NOT pinned: the
;; MIC register measured this same shell at 696 bytes, so it moves on its own
;; and a check keyed to it would report the host wrong for a reason that means
;; nothing.
;;
;; So the host is declared :indistinguishable, page checks on it are REFUSED,
;; and every statute is resolved through the law API instead. The
;; indistinguishability is re-measured every run; if the host ever starts
;; telling the two apart, this rule has expired and that is what notices.
;;
;; ── LAW IDS WERE NOT DERIVABLE AND WERE NOT GUESSED
;;
;; Every :egov/law-id below came back from a title query against the law API,
;; not from a pattern. The guesses that were tried and failed are worth
;; recording: 322AC0000000018 (the pre-2007 統計法) and 327AC0000000148
;; (統計報告調整法) both return total_count 0 -- they are not in the API at
;; all, so a repealed-statute control could not be built from the obvious
;; candidates and had to be found by enumerating the 43 instruments whose title
;; contains 統計.
;;
;; ── PAGE PATHS WERE NOT DERIVABLE EITHER
;;
;; Also worth recording, because the paths look systematic and are not.
;; Measured 404 on the first attempt: /index/seido/index.html,
;; /index/seido/houki.htm, /index/seido/houki.html, /index/seido/1-1.html on
;; www.stat.go.jp, and /toukei_toukatsu/index/seido/index.htm,
;; /toukei_toukatsu/index/seido/houkoku.htm, /toukei_toukatsu/index/seido/1-1k.htm
;; and /toukei_toukatsu/index/index.html on www.soumu.go.jp. Every URL below
;; was read off a link on a page that was itself fetched.
;;
;; ── DATES HERE ARE UTC
;;
;; :source/retrieved-at is the UTC date of the fetch. This workstation runs
;; JST, so a date copied from `date` without -u is nine hours ahead and would
;; make a retrieval look newer than it is.
;;
;; ── WHAT :source/covers CLAIMS, AND WHERE IT STOPS
;;
;; An entry establishes that the instrument or page EXISTS, is identified as
;; written, and is in the force status declared. It does not establish what any
;; provision says. register.coverage lists what is deliberately not here.

[
 ;; ── What this register does not cover ──────────────────────────────────────
 {:source/id "register.coverage"
  :source/kind :coverage
  :coverage/entries 30
  :coverage/by-verify {:e-gov-law-id 18 :page-text 12}
  :coverage/measured-at "2026-08-27"
  :coverage/excludes
  #{;; Article text. Nothing below asserts what any provision SAYS -- only
    ;; that the instrument exists, is identified as written, and is in the
    ;; force status declared. A requirement checklist built on this register
    ;; still has to read the provision.
    :article-text
    ;; The 承認 / 届出 split itself. Whether a survey an operator is caught by
    ;; is a 基幹統計調査, a 一般統計調査 or a 届出統計調査 is the first question
    ;; this repository is asked, and it is decided by 統計法 together with
    ;; 統計法施行令's designations. Both are cited; the classification of any
    ;; particular survey is not established by citing them.
    :survey-classification
    ;; Whether a named operator is a designated respondent for a given survey,
    ;; and on what cycle. The survey ordinances are cited; no operator's
    ;; enumeration status is.
    :respondent-designation
    ;; The 調査票 forms themselves, their fields and their filing deadlines.
    ;; Those move on each survey's own timetable and none are carried here.
    :survey-forms-and-deadlines
    ;; Eligibility to receive 調査票情報 under 統計法. The microdata portal and
    ;; the ministry's activation page are cited; who may actually be granted
    ;; access, and on what terms, is not.
    :microdata-eligibility
    ;; Penalties. 統計法 carries criminal provisions for false reporting and for
    ;; disclosure of survey information; no amount or exposure is stated here.
    :penalties
    ;; Subnational instruments. Prefectures and municipalities run statistical
    ;; work under their own rules, and none of those are here.
    :subnational-instruments}}

